Lie Groups and Differentiable Manifolds, Mathematics Parts C and B; Wednesday 28 May 2008, 9.30am–12.30pm. The complete four-page source and both sections are privately transcribed from original Part C bundle pages 117–120, supplied through https://www.whatdotheyknow.com/request/maths_past_papers_3[the past-papers disclosure]. No exact worked-answer advertisement was found in the bounded availability check. Representations are finite-dimensional and continuous; manifolds have no boundary unless stated otherwise.

